{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790980631,"nonce":"X8CaesduUF9NSE10C2WLO4Q9508=","title":"Animated offscreen rendering, after a motion system","message":"Offscreen (7643b7d) ports BlincApp's static paths: render, render_tree, render_to_texture, render_to_rgba8, read_texture_to_rgba8. Blinc also has render_to_texture_with_motion / render_to_rgba8_with_motion (blinc_app/src/app.rs ~308-370): the motion-aware path the windowed runner uses, with springs, motion containers, transform animations and the motion-bake overlay, driven by a caller-owned RenderState whose AnimationScheduler the caller ticks per frame (deterministic video export: tick dt, render frame N, push to encoder).\n\nashui has no motion or animation system yet, so there is nothing to port. When one exists, add the matching Offscreen methods taking the caller's animation state, so headless export and image-diff tests of animated UI work without a window.","files":null}]}